The "MCP":https://modelcontextprotocol.io/ server now offers the tools @whoami@ (the user the request authenticates as, with their groups) and @get_permissions@ (the user's permissions on an object or an object type, as named flags). A failed tool call now also returns a structured @problem@ (type, status, whether a retry may help, and the CMS response code and messages), next to its error text, so that a client can tell for example a page locked by another user from a missing permission.
